---
// Utils
import { Picture, getImage } from "astro:assets";

// Components
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Banner from "@components/Banner/Banner.astro";
import Stats from "@components/Stats/stats.astro";
import CTA from "@components/CTA/CTASimple.astro";

// Images
import landingImage from "@assets/images/landing.jpg"; // <-- THE PATH TO THE ASSET YOU WANT TO PRELOAD - The asset must live in src
const optimizedImage = await getImage({ src: landingImage, format: "webp" });

import DrivewayIMG1 from "@assets/images/services/driveway1.jpeg";
import DrivewayIMG2 from "@assets/images/services/driveway2.jpeg";
import DrivewayIMG3 from "@assets/images/services/driveway3.jpeg";
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Driveway Pressure Washing in Jacksonville, FL | Pristine Patio Pros"
	description="Professional driveway pressure washing in Jacksonville. Remove stains, mold & buildup from concrete and paver driveways. 15% off first service. Free quote!"
	heroImage={optimizedImage}
>
	<Banner title="Driveway Pressure Washing" image={optimizedImage} />

	<!-- SBS 1 -->
	<section id="sbs-2316">
		<div class="cs-container">
			<div class="cs-content cs-content1">
				<Picture
					src={DrivewayIMG1}
					alt="concrete driveway being pressured washed"
					width={608}
					formats={["avif", "webp"]}
					pictureAttributes={{ class: "cs-picture cs-picture1" }}
				/>
				<div class="cs-wrapper cs-wrapper1">
					<h1 class="cs-title">
						Driveway Pressure Washing in Jacksonville, FL
					</h1>
					<p class="cs-text">
						Driveways are often the first thing noticed when someone pulls up to
						your property, and in Jacksonville's climate they take a beating
						from dirt, tire marks, mildew, and organic growth faster than most
						surfaces. Driveway pressure washing tackles that buildup directly,
						focusing on concrete and similar hard surfaces to remove
						surface-level staining, algae, and mildew and restore a cleaner,
						more even appearance. Adjacent areas affected by overspray are
						rinsed down as part of the process, so the surrounding space is left
						tidy when the work is done. Before any cleaning starts, the driveway
						and surrounding area are walked and assessed so cracks, slopes,
						parked vehicles, and nearby plants are noted and accounted for. That
						upfront check is what keeps the work focused and prevents surprises
						for both sides.
					</p>
					<!-- <ul class="cs-ul">
						<strong>What's Included?</strong>
						<li class="cs-li">
							Pressure washing of concrete and similar hard driveway surfaces
						</li>
						<li class="cs-li">
							Focus on removing surface-level staining, algae, and mildew
						</li>
						<li class="cs-li">
							Rinsing of adjacent areas affected by overspray where appropriate
						</li>
					</ul> -->
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<!-- 3-Card -->
	<section id="services-1331">
		<div class="cs-container">
			<h2 class="cs-h2">Benefits of a Clean Driveway</h2>
			<ul class="cs-card-group">
				<li class="cs-item">
					<div class="cs-link">
						<h3 class="cs-h3">Safer Surfaces Underfoot</h3>
						<p class="cs-item-text">
							Mold, mildew, and algae build up on driveway surfaces faster in
							Jacksonville's climate than most homeowners expect. Over time that
							organic growth creates slippery patches that are a real hazard for
							anyone walking or pulling into the driveway. A pressure wash
							clears it out and leaves the surface safer to use day to day.
						</p>
					</div>
				</li>
				<li class="cs-item">
					<div class="cs-link">
						<h3 class="cs-h3">A Cleaner First Impression</h3>
						<p class="cs-item-text">
							The driveway is one of the first things people notice when they
							pull up to your property. Staining, discoloration, and buildup can
							make an otherwise well-kept home look neglected from the street.
							Cleaning it restores an even, maintained appearance that reflects
							well on the rest of the property.
						</p>
					</div>
				</li>
				<li class="cs-item">
					<div class="cs-link">
						<h3 class="cs-h3">Long-Term Surface Protection</h3>
						<p class="cs-item-text">
							Concrete and pavers are durable, but the buildup that sits on them
							over time works against that durability. Organic growth and
							trapped moisture break down the surface material gradually,
							leading to cracks and deterioration that cost real money to
							repair. Regular cleaning is one of the simpler ways to protect
							that investment and extend the life of the surface.
						</p>
					</div>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</div>
	</section>

	<Stats />

	<section id="sbs-1565">
		<div class="cs-container">
			<Picture
				src={DrivewayIMG3}
				alt="concrete driveway being pressured washed"
				width={586}
				formats={["avif", "webp"]}
				pictureAttributes={{ class: "cs-picture" }}
			/>
			<div class="cs-content">
				<span class="cs-topper">How driveway cleaning works</span>
				<h2 class="cs-title">Driveway Cleaning Process</h2>
				<ul class="cs-card-group">
					<li class="cs-li">
						<div class="cs-flex">
							<h3 class="cs-h3">Inspect Driveway and Surroundings</h3>
							<p class="cs-li-text">
								The driveway surface is first reviewed so cracks, stains,
								slopes, drainage paths, parked vehicles, garage doors, and
								nearby plants are noted. This helps prevent surprises and guides
								how water and cleaning solutions are directed during the work.
								Loose material such as sand, dirt, leaves, and small stones is
								cleared from the driveway so the pressure washing can focus on
								bonded buildup rather than surface clutter. Items that can be
								moved safely are set aside to keep the work area open.
							</p>
						</div>
					</li>
					<li class="cs-li">
						<div class="cs-flex">
							<h3 class="cs-h3">Apply Pressure and Solution</h3>
							<p class="cs-li-text">
								Pressure levels, spray tips, and cleaning solutions are selected
								according to the driveway material and visible buildup. A
								cleaner may be applied to help break down organic growth, tire
								marks, and general staining before the main rinse begins. This
								service is not intended for oil stains, rust, or tine shine
								removal, and does not include landscape curbing.
							</p>
						</div>
					</li>
					<li class="cs-li">
						<div class="cs-flex">
							<h3 class="cs-h3">Rinse and Check Results</h3>
							<p class="cs-li-text">
								The driveway is rinsed in steady, overlapping passes from the
								higher areas toward the lower ones so dirty water is carried
								away. Remaining marks are checked and addressed where possible,
								and edges are rinsed to leave the surrounding area more even in
								appearance.
							</p>
						</div>
					</li>
				</ul>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>

	<CTA />
</BaseLayout>

<!-- SBS 1 Styles -->
<style lang="less">
	/*-- -------------------------- -->
<!--        Side by Side        -->
<--- -------------------------- -*/

	/* Mobile - 360px */
	@media only screen and (min-width: 0rem) {
		#sbs-2316 {
			padding: var(--sectionPadding);
			position: relative;

			.cs-container {
				width: 100%;
				/* changes to 1280px at tablet */
				max-width: (584/16rem);
				margin: auto;
				display: flex;
				flex-direction: column;
				align-items: center;
				/* 48px - 64px */
				gap: clamp(3rem, 10vw, 4rem);
			}

			.cs-content {
				/* set text align to center if content needs to be centrally aligned */
				text-align: left;
				width: 100%;
				display: flex;
				flex-direction: column;
				/* aligns content to the left, set to center to centrally align */
				align-items: flex-start;
				/* 48px - 72px */
				gap: clamp(3rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
			}

			.cs-content2 {
				/* 20px - 72px */
				gap: clamp(1.25rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
			}

			.cs-title,
			.cs-text {
				max-width: 100%;
			}

			.cs-ul {
				margin: (16/16rem) 0 (32/16rem) 0;
				padding: 0;
				display: flex;
				flex-direction: column;
				gap: (12/16rem);
			}

			.cs-li {
				font-size: (16/16rem);
				line-height: 1.5em;
				list-style: none;
				color: var(--bodyTextColor);

				&:before {
					/* bullet */
					content: "";
					width: (8/16rem);
					height: (8/16rem);
					margin: 0 (12/16rem) (2/16rem) (2/16rem);
					background: var(--secondary);
					display: inline-block;
					transform: rotate(45deg);
				}
			}

			.cs-button-box {
				width: 100%;
				display: flex;
				justify-content: flex-start;
				align-items: center;
				flex-wrap: wrap;
				column-gap: (32/16rem);
				row-gap: (16/16rem);
			}

			.cs-link {
				text-decoration: none;
				display: flex;
				justify-content: flex-start;
				align-items: center;
				gap: (16/16rem);
				position: relative;
			}

			.cs-icon-wrapper {
				width: (60/16rem);
				height: (60/16rem);
				display: flex;
				justify-content: center;
				align-items: center;
				position: relative;
				transition: transform 0.3s;
				/* prevents flexbox from squishing it */
				flex: none;

				&::before {
					content: "";
					width: 100%;
					height: 100%;
					background-color: var(--primary);
					opacity: 0.05;
					position: absolute;
					top: 0;
					left: 0;
					z-index: -1;
				}
			}

			.cs-icon {
				width: (24/16rem);
				height: auto;
				display: block;
			}

			.cs-info {
				display: flex;
				flex-direction: column;
				align-items: flex-start;
				gap: (4/16rem);
			}

			.cs-link-content {
				font-size: (16/16rem);
				font-weight: 400;
				line-height: 1.2em;
				margin: 0;
				color: var(--bodyTextColor);
				display: block;
			}

			.cs-phone {
				font-size: (25/16rem);
				font-weight: 700;
				line-height: 1.2em;
				margin: 0;
				color: var(--headerColor);
				display: block;
			}

			.cs-img {
				width: (60/16rem);
				height: auto;
			}

			.cs-signature {
				width: auto;
				height: (36/16rem);
				/* centers the signature while everything else remains aligned to the left */
				margin: 0 auto;
				display: block;
			}

			.cs-job {
				font-size: (16/16rem);
				line-height: 1.5em;
				text-align: center;
				margin-top: (6/16rem);
				padding-top: (4/16rem);
				color: var(--bodyTextColor);
				border-top: 1px solid #e7e7e8;
			}

			.cs-button-solid {
				font-size: (16/16rem);
				font-weight: 700;
				/* 46px - 56px */
				line-height: clamp(2.875rem, 5.5vw, 3.5rem);
				text-align: center;
				text-decoration: none;
				min-width: (150/16rem);
				margin: (32/16rem) 0 0;
				/* prevents padding from adding to the width */
				box-sizing: border-box;
				padding: 0 (24/16rem);
				background-color: var(--primary);
				color: #fff;
				border-radius: (4/16rem);
				display: inline-block;
				position: relative;
				z-index: 1;

				&:before {
					content: "";
					width: 0%;
					height: 100%;
					background: #000;
					opacity: 1;
					border-radius: (4/16rem);
					position: absolute;
					top: 0;
					left: 0;
					z-index: -1;
					transition: width 0.3s;
				}

				&:hover {
					&:before {
						width: 100%;
					}
				}
			}

			.cs-picture {
				display: block;
				position: relative;
				z-index: 1;

				img {
					width: 100%;
					height: 100%;
					object-fit: cover;
					position: absolute;
					top: 0;
					left: 0;
					box-shadow: 10px 10px 0px -4px #000000;
					border-radius: 0.75rem;
				}
			}

			.cs-picture1 {
				width: 100%;
				/* 280px - 400px */
				height: clamp(17.5rem, 55vw, 25rem);
			}

			.cs-picture2 {
				width: 100%;
				height: (280/16rem);
			}
		}
	}

	/* Desktop - 1024px */
	@media only screen and (min-width: 64rem) {
		#sbs-2316 {
			.cs-container {
				max-width: (1280/16rem);
				flex-direction: column;
				justify-content: space-between;
				align-items: stretch;
			}

			.cs-content {
				flex-direction: row;
				align-items: stretch;
				justify-content: space-between;
			}

			.cs-content2 {
				flex-direction: row-reverse;
				justify-content: space-between;
			}

			.cs-wrapper {
				width: 100%;
				max-width: (795/16rem);
			}

			.cs-wrapper2 {
				max-width: (413/16rem);
				padding-bottom: (120/16rem);
			}

			.cs-picture1 {
				max-width: (412/16rem);
				height: auto;
			}

			.cs-picture2 {
				width: 64vw;
				max-width: (795/16rem);
				height: auto;
				flex: none;
			}
		}
	}

	/* Large Desktop - 1300px */
	@media only screen and (min-width: 81.25rem) {
		#sbs-2316 {
			.cs-wrapper {
				padding-right: (72/16rem);
			}
		}
	}

	/* Dark Mode */
	@media only screen and (min-width: 0rem) {
		body.dark-mode {
			#sbs-2316 {
				.cs-title,
				.cs-text,
				.cs-li,
				.cs-link-content,
				.cs-phone,
				.cs-job {
					color: var(--bodyTextColorWhite);
				}

				.cs-text,
				.cs-li,
				.cs-link-content,
				.cs-job {
					opacity: 0.8;
				}

				.cs-icon-wrapper {
					&::before {
						background-color: var(--medium);
						opacity: 1;
					}
				}

				.cs-signature {
					filter: invert(1) brightness(100%);
				}
			}
		}
	}
</style>

<!-- 3-Card -->
